{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under **Rule 6c-11(d)**, a US ETF must preserve:\n\n- **AP agreements:** All written agreements—or copies—with authorized participants permitting orders to purchase or redeem creation units.\n- **Each exchanged basket:** Records showing:\n  - Each holding’s ticker symbol, CUSIP or other identifier; description; quantity; and percentage weight in the basket.\n  - The identity of the AP conducting the transaction.\n  - If applicable, a statement identifying the basket as a **custom basket**, plus a record stating that it complies with the ETF’s policies and procedures adopted under Rule 6c-11(c)(3).\n  - Any cash balancing amount.\n\n**Retention:** Both categories must be maintained and preserved for **at least five years**, with the **first two years in an easily accessible place**."}}
